{\b Voice input in Perekey uses these open models and libraries. The models run on your Mac.}\par
{\b Speech recognition.} NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (NVIDIA) and Parakeet Ultra (a post-training of it by Moondream), licensed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}}{\fldrslt CC BY 4.0}}, converted to Core ML by Fluid Inference. The converted files are modified.\par
{\b Whisper.} OpenAI Whisper large-v3 turbo, MIT License, as Core ML files from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://huggingface.co/argmaxinc/whisperkit-coreml"}}{\fldrslt argmaxinc/whisperkit-coreml}}. Its tokenizer files come from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-large-v3"}}{\fldrslt openai/whisper-large-v3}} (Apache License 2.0).\par
{\b Voice activity.} Silero VAD, MIT License, converted to Core ML by Fluid Inference.\par
{\b Speakers.} The diarization of FluidAudio uses models from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml"}}{\fldrslt FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml}} ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}}{\fldrslt CC BY 4.0}}): pyannote segmentation-community-1 (pyannote.audio), WeSpeaker ResNet34 embeddings (WeSpeaker), VBx clustering and PLDA (BUT Speech@FIT), converted to Core ML and changed by Fluid Inference.\par
{\b Libraries.} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio"}}{\fldrslt FluidAudio}} (Apache License 2.0), with fastcluster (BSD 2-Clause, Daniel M\u252?llner and Google) and a Japanese text frontend ported from Misaki (Apache License 2.0), cutlet and Convert-Numbers-to-Japanese (MIT). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/argmaxinc/argmax-oss-swift"}}{\fldrslt WhisperKit}} (MIT License), with parts derived from swift-transformers by Hugging Face (Apache License 2.0).\par
{\b Updates.} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sparkle-project.org"}}{\fldrslt Sparkle}} (MIT License), with bsdiff by Colin Percival, sais-lite by Yuta Mori, Ed25519 by Orson Peters and SUSignatureVerifier by Mark Hamlin; their terms are in the LICENSE file of Sparkle.\par
